{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/382506-need-help-pronto-world-of-darkness-ireland-mta-ctd-wta","id":382506,"title":"Need help pronto: World of Darkness Ireland. MtA/CtD/WtA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-26T17:37:49-08:00","id":382506,"title":"Need help pronto: World of Darkness Ireland. MtA/CtD/WtA","content":"im running a campaing and suddenly i face slammed onto a corner.<br /> basically, one of my PC is hunting two nephandi who are in Ireland, apparently they are looking for Something involving the End of the World. right now my PC meet a group of garous (didnt end up well) and he knows this might be involving Fae.<br /> <br /> the catch is...i like to keep my games as close to the cannon as possible and now i realized i dont know anything on how Ireland is portrayed on the WoD and about Faes on the area, can someone help me out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T18:00:44-08:00","id":382541,"title":"","content":"Why worry about Changeling the game when you have mythology at hand. They say the Fomorians, a evil race of conquering evil giants, led by the terrible Balor One-Eyed were banished by the early heroes of Ireland. The Fianna even claim they had a hand in imprisoning them. Now the Nephandi seek to free the Fomorians and pledge their allegiance to Balor. The Mages have to find a common tongue with the Garou and possibly some Fae helping or hindering both casts - one group does not want to see the Fomorians back, and the other feels that the Fomorians are just deserts for the terrible, terrible humans. (you really don't have to use Changeling the game to run a fun Mage chronicle with Fae)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T18:23:03-08:00","id":382554,"title":"","content":"where can i find info on the Fomorians? as for their stats and such","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T18:28:24-08:00","id":382557,"title":"","content":"Errh. Invent something? Wikipedia has a lovely article on them? Slaine had a pretty damn awesome arc about the war between the protoIrish and the Fomorians? Go crazy, have fun with creating cool monsters. Make Balor a suave one eyed bastard that loves fine silk suits and drops people dead with one look, or just make the Fomorians into alien entities with little concepts similar to humanity? Make them the Gods of the Nephandi which they will worship and who will gift them with ancient magics and lost alchemies... or make them dumb slaves who will serve as the bruisers of the Nephandi who freed them.<br /> <br /> You don't need stats to create something unique and special as a threat.<br /> <br /> ... but if you really have to go by the book, one version of the Fomorians appears in the Apocalypse book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T18:44:03-08:00","id":382562,"title":"","content":"so far the main twist i got its that, my PC is hunting two nephandi..but they are a couple, and one of them is pregnant (the childe is another nephandi) so i was thinking on making the child the Balor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T04:30:27-08:00","id":382919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/382506-need-help-pronto-world-of-darkness-ireland-mta-ctd-wta?p=382562#post382562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so far the main twist i got its that, my PC is hunting two nephandi..but they are a couple, and one of them is pregnant (the childe is another nephandi) so i was thinking on making the child the Balor</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so let's go from there. Maybe they used an ancient rite to free the spirit of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balor\" target=\"_blank\">Balor</a> throught the female becoming pregnant with him and reincarnating him into our world as the usher of the end of days and for him to free the other <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fomorians\" target=\"_blank\">Fomorians</a> from deep under the Earth. They are running to Ireland to have the birth of the newborn Balor in a place hallowed to the Fomorians... maybe the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant%27s_Causeway\" target=\"_blank\">Giant's Causeway</a>? Maybe an ancient cave where the Fomorians held court? Or a long lost city under the water? A haunted legendary circle of stones hewn by giants before the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuatha_D%C3%A9_Danann\" target=\"_blank\">Tuatha De Danan</a> and men cast them out? In this place the newborn Balor will be born under auspicious circumstances and given vast powers and dark blessings that will usher in him as the bringer of the Apocalypse and the freer of his race from unjust imprisonment. Maybe they seek a deep, dark cave that has not seen the Sun in millenia, and as the newborn Balor exits the womb of his dark mother, he cracks the walls that imprison the fomorians? Maybe Balor grows up faster then he should, or comes out of the Nephandi fully grown (ouch, this can end up quite squicky if you want it to).<br /> <br /> You could easily have Balor freed and let loose upon the world of men while the Nephandi are left dead or neutralysed and have the Mages face a cunning new horror in the world. They may have to find a common tongue with the local druids and witches (some Celtic Verbena offshoot probably) without being set alight within a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wicker_man\" target=\"_blank\">Wicker Man</a> or maybe make peace with the Fianna long enough to fight off this horrible monstrosity that will usher the end of days...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:01:20-08:00","id":383113,"title":"","content":"Immortal Eyes: Court of All Kings is the Changeling sourcebook for Ireland. In C:tD, the Fomorians fill the same space as Vampire's antediluvians. They are essentially plot devices. You won't find stats for them.<br /> <br /> Asmodai has great advice though. It sounds like you're running a primarily Mage game. Stick with that. Use the mythology and mine the other games for ideas to make an awesome Mage plot, but don't worry too much about the details of Werewolf: The Apocalypse or Changeling: The Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:14:06-08:00","id":383215,"title":"","content":"<i>Dreams and Nightmares</i> (a sourcebook about the Dreaming for Changeling) cover some info about Fomorians, if you want to get more specific WoD canon lore about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/n6g3njp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/kpa5GS5Mp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/93820aaad7.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/584-eliseo-ap-liam","name":"Eliseo ap Liam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T03:46:26-08:00","id":384075,"title":"","content":"I would agree on the Don't Worry about Changeling thing. Much as I love it the Mage cosmos is big enough that you don't need it and the Myths and Legends are a far stronger resource if there is no real crossover going on (Werewolf I think it;s fine to stick closer too as there is a lot of cosmological Cross Over between the two lines in terms of Umbra and Realms). To build on the suggestions given, the sacred place of the Formorians is Tory Isle and don't forget they have associations with the Winter and the Sea (Balor originally being the son of Domnu and Mannan Mac Lir, also brother to Crom the lord of Autumn, Rot and Decay). It's also worth noting that Balor was more than just a tyrant with a killing eye, he was a hero of his people and spoke with a bard's blessing. Evil? Certainly, a Cruel destroyer of people? Yes, but still rather likeable in person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T04:12:26-08:00","id":384091,"title":"","content":"If You are searching for Fomorians , You should read comics Slaine especially draw by Simon Bisley, there You'll find Balor and other fomorians, a lot of interesting stories and Celtic myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T09:48:10-08:00","id":384298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/382506-need-help-pronto-world-of-darkness-ireland-mta-ctd-wta?p=384075#post384075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To build on the suggestions given, the sacred place of the Formorians is Tory Isle and don't forget they have associations with the Winter and the Sea (Balor originally being the son of Domnu and Mannan Mac Lir, also brother to Crom the lord of Autumn, Rot and Decay). It's also worth noting that Balor was more than just a tyrant with a killing eye, he was a hero of his people and spoke with a bard's blessing. Evil? Certainly, a Cruel destroyer of people? Yes, but still rather likeable in person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you find that information on Irish mythology? I went through all my sources and I could not find anything relating Balor directly to Mannannan (who may not be of the core families of the Tuatha who came down out of Tir Nan Og,, but seems to have a lot more to do with them than he does with the Formorians). Admittedly, parentage and descent in Irish mythology is often quite insane, but that one would definitely put a lot of stories in a very different light. Mannannan is usually seen as a good father, but, if Balor is his son, then he's a complete shit to him... sending adventurers in to steal Balor's (stolen) cow and make off with this daughter, raising the kid that is destined to kill his own son, etc. <br /> <br /> Crom, in as much as he is associated with anyone in particular, has always seemed more associated with the Fir Bolg as opposed to the Fomorians. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T16:07:21-08:00","id":384586,"title":"","content":"Fragments over the years more than anything. Don't forget that much of the Celtic myth otherworld tilts on an axis of perception. CuChulain after all is a massive hero in one direction and a blood soaked monster in the other. Math is wise, just and great but also full of hubris and utterly inflexible. Lugh is heroic and noble but also inattentive of his wife. Danu herself is magnificent but utterly contradictory and fickle. Morrigan is wicked and cruel and yet also a warning that may be heeded to avoid ill fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T21:31:40-08:00","id":387997,"title":"","content":"Echoing what other people have said: make up what fits your story. Golden rule golden rule. However, if you someday want to revisit this setting and just want to be more familiar, here are your answers:<br /> <br /> -For the Fae and Mage presence (to include locations of canon chantrys) in England, Scotland and Wales &quot;Isle of Mighty&quot; is your sourcebook (starting at page 15, with some special attention on page 21 as it goes a long way towards explaining why there are no more Dark Ages Fae). They do not cover Ireland, I find the Fianna tribe book to be of more help there.<br /> <br /> -For the Formorians see &quot;Denizens of the Dreaming&quot;. They were hot shit a thousand years ago but have since been relegated to the Deep and Far Dreaming.<br /> <br /> -Naughty naughty Balor One-Eye left a line of Fae. For information on them, check out the sourcebooks<br /> &quot;Pour L'Amour et Liberte: The Book of Houses 2&quot; (starting on page 103), &quot;The Shadow Court&quot; (page 63) and &quot;Book of Lost Dreams&quot; (from pages 42-43)<br /> <br /> -&quot;Noblesse Oblige&quot; is a sourcebook on the sidhe changeling &quot;house&quot; of Fiona, who have many ancient pacts and frequently share progeny with the Fianna.<br /> <br /> -Furthermore, here is a listing of how the British fae have divided up their dream lands:<br /> <br /> Albion (England)<br /> The Kingdom of Chalk: The South of England.<br /> The Kingdom of Mist: The Southwest of England.<br /> The Kingdom of Roses: From London to Just below the Midlands, encompassing Anglia.<br /> The Kingdom of Smoke: The Midlands.<br /> The Kingdom of Heather: The North of England.<br /> <br /> Caledonia (Scotland)<br /> The kingdom of the Three Hills: From Hadrian's Wall to just below Edinburg.<br /> The Tuath of Dew: Edinburg and surrounding area.<br /> The Tuath of Iron: The Southwest of Scotland.<br /> The Tuath of Shadow: The Northwest of Scotland.<br /> The Cridhe: The Scottish Highlands.<br /> The Kingdom of Alba: The East Coast of Scotland.<br /> <br /> Cymru (Wales)<br /> Gwynt: South East.<br /> Glamorgan: South.<br /> Dyfed: Southwest.<br /> Powys: middle.<br /> Clnyd: Northeast.<br /> Gwynedd: Northwest.<br /> Ynysman: Island just off of the northwest coast.<br /> <br /> So as you can see, this is a ton of reading. Think on it if you really want to get into canon. Again, if you want to revisit this for future chronicles this would be helpful, but otherwise I just see it as work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","user":"Sarah RPs","date":". 02-01-2015, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T21:37:37-08:00","id":388000,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all for the help!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}